id: pm-gh1644
title: "GH-1644: context --for orient silently reduces an explicit --limit to the intent's budget-derived row ceiling, and pm's own quickstart recommends that command"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1644\n\nReproduced on the current source build (2026.10.31) in a fresh 6-task sandbox and on the real tracker: `pm context --limit 10 --for orient` returns filters.limit \"3\" in either flag order, while `pm context --limit 10` returns 10. The intent applier (CONTEXT_INTENT_DEFAULT_APPLIERS in src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts) computes a budget-derived ceiling ((3000 - 1200) / 600 = 3 rows) and replaces the caller's --limit with min(requested, derived). The context_intent receipt reports binding_constraint token_budget but neither the requested value nor a warning; filters.limit shows only the effective 3. list --for triage and search --for discover use the same clamp.\n\nMeasured on the real tracker (3173 items): 3 orient rows serialize to ~1,680 JSON tokens, 5 rows ~2,724, 10 rows ~5,937. The 3000-token preset therefore genuinely cannot carry 10 rows, so the preset ceiling is correct; the defects are (1) the silent override, (2) filters reporting only the effective value, and (3) pm's own agent quickstart (init-agent-guidance, AGENTS.md, README, AGENT_GUIDE) recommending `pm context --limit 10 --for orient`, a self-contradicting command. The measured canonical in token-budget-gate is `context --for orient` without --limit.\n\nDuplicate search: 'context orient preset limit', 'for orient intent preset', GH-1644; nearest are pm-gy885b (intent discoverability, closed), pm-3crymx (intent returned no context, closed) and pm-ka6d (canonical cold-start docs, closed)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,context,github,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-10-31T21:13:36.728Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T23:02:09.740Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:33.693Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:33.693Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "An explicit row limit above the intent's budget-derived ceiling yields a typed limit_overridden_by_intent warning naming --limit, the requested and effective values, and a --token-budget that would carry the request; filters reports requested_limit beside the effective limit whenever they differ; the context_intent receipt records requested_limit; the same behaviour holds for context, list --for triage and search --for discover; generated agent guidance, AGENTS.md, README and docs recommend the measured canonical pm context --for orient; a regression test covers every row-bounded intent with an explicit over-ceiling limit"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "The three row-bounded intent appliers share applyIntentRowLimit, which keeps the budget-derived ceiling and records a reduced request. attachContextIntentReceipt writes context_intent.limit_override {flag, requested, effective, token_budget_for_requested, restore_with}, filters.requested_limit, and the warning limit_overridden_by_intent:--limit N->M for context, list and search intents, reading either projected or raw host options. The quickstart generator, AGENTS.md, README, AGENT_GUIDE, COMMAND_NAMESPACES, the pm-user skill reference and both replayed agent-task transcripts use pm context --for orient. The quickstart no longer calls explicit --start atomic."
expected_result: Every row-bounded --for intent either honours an explicit --limit or reports a typed override with the requested and effective values and a retry that keeps the limit; pm's quickstart recommends no silently overridden flag.
actual_result: "Real tracker: pm context --for orient --limit 10 prints filters.requested_limit 10 beside limit 3, the warning, and restore_with pm context --for orient --limit 10 --token-budget 7200. That retry returns 10 rows at 4,637 estimated tokens within budget. list --for triage --limit 150 discloses 150->100. The agent-task token baseline changed only its transcript digest (identical output). intent-limit-override spec 3/3 passes; 3/3 fail with the fix stashed."
