comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-31T21:46:59.575Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation: the three row-bounded intent appliers share applyIntentRowLimit, which keeps the existing min(requested, budget-derived) clamp but stashes a reduced request as intentRequestedLimit. attachContextIntentReceipt calls discloseIntentLimitOverride, which reads that key or the raw host --limit and writes context_intent.limit_override {flag, requested, effective, token_budget_for_requested, restore_with}, filters.requested_limit, and the warning 'limit_overridden_by_intent:--limit N->M'. token_budget_for_requested = max(current budget, overhead + rowCost*requested) from the shared resolveIntentRowCost table. Measured on this tracker: pm context --for orient --limit 10 now prints the override with restore_with 'pm context --for orient --limit 10 --token-budget 7200'. That retry returns 10 rows at an estimated 4,637 tokens within budget. list --for triage --limit 150 → effective 100, retry with --token-budget 3200 honours 150. The quickstart (init-agent-guidance, AGENTS.md, README, AGENT_GUIDE, COMMAND_NAMESPACES, pm-user ECOSYSTEM_PLANNING) and the replayed agent-task transcript now use the measured canonical pm context --for orient."
  "2026-10-31T23:02:09.739Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 1 on PR #1645: limit_override.restore_with is now the flag fragment '--token-budget N' to add to (or replace in) the original command, following the omission-receipt convention (restore_with '--full'). The full rebuilt command had dropped named options (--status, --sort) and inline search field:value filters. token_budget_for_requested and restore_with are omitted when the sufficient budget is not a safe integer (spec covers Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER)."
